/*!

\mainpage 


The AlamDMC program provides a way to perform a stress-driven analysis by means of micro-mechanical models, such as the Full Constraint Taylor or the Alamel, which typically are strain-rate driven.


This manual is divided into three parts.

The first part forms a user manual:
<ul>

<li> Section \ref page_gettingstarted tells you how to run the software and demonstrates the various ways that code can
     be used.
<li> Section \ref page_configuration explains in detail what input has to be provided by the user: configuration files and input data.   
<li> Section \ref theory  contains  a brief overview how the software operates and how the quantities of interest are calculated.
</ul>

*/


